ets founding father Rufus King's political legacy and antislavery history to teach critical thinking for a healthier democracy.","contact_name":"Kelsey Brow","email":"director@kingmanor.org","phone":"718.206.0545","website":"kingmanor.org","social":"Facebook: @kingmanormuseum; Instagram: @kingmanormuseum","languages":"English, French, Spanish","accepts_referrals":"Yes","fees":"Not usually","source":"qnpd","provenance":"queens_nonprofit_directory_v3","verified_on":"8/28/26"},{"resource_id":"qnpd:legal-services-nyc-queens","name":"Legal Services NYC/Queens","category":"benefits-and-legal","subcategory":"Legal Services","is_coad_member":false,"lon":-73.808922,"lat":40.703485,"address":"89-00 Sutphin Blvd., 5th Floor, Jamaica, NY 11435","mission":"Queens Legal Services, a program of Legal Services NYC, is a civil legal services organization with a mission to fight poverty and seek racial, social, and economic justice on behalf of low-income New Yorkers. We are a part of Legal Services NYC, which has offices in each borough. We provide a wide range of civil legal services and balance individual case representation, impact litigation and policy advocacy, community outreach, education, and training. We do landlord/tenant; disability (Social Security Disability/SSI/ Retirement Benefits); Medicaid and Medicare Issues; SNAP; Public Benefits; Unemployment & Wage Issues; Discrimination based on protected class; Family Court cases; Domestic Violence; Foreclosure; Consumer Issues; Tax issues; Veterans cases; and LGBTQ+/HIV Advocacy issues. We are glad to do Know-Your-Rights presentations for your organization and your clients on any legal issues we cover.","contact_name":"William Flynn","email":"wtflynn@lsnyc.org","phone":"347.592.2254","website":"LSNYC.org","social":"Instagram: @legalservicesnyc","languages":"All languages - we utilize Language Line as well as having in-house interpreters in Spanish; Mandarin; Bengali; and Arabic.","accepts_referrals":"Yes","fees":"None","source